# YAML 1.2
# https://citation-file-format.github.io/
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the SkillLens paper (arXiv preprint
  forthcoming). Replace the placeholder author list below with the canonical
  author block once the arXiv submission is finalized.
title: >-
  SkillLens: From Task-First Evaluation to Skill-Centered Assessment
authors:
  # FIXME: replace with the real author list before public announcement.
  - name: "SkillLens-AI Contributors"
date-released: "2026-05-07"
url: "https://skilllens-ai.github.io/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/SkillLens-AI/skilllens"
license: Apache-2.0
type: software
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.20253170
    description: Companion dataset on Zenodo (CDLA-Permissive-2.0).
keywords:
  - large-language-models
  - agent-evaluation
  - skill-assessment
  - benchmark
  - llm-agents
abstract: >-
  SkillLens is an evaluation framework that measures the incremental
  task-completion gain that an Anthropic-style /skill markdown file
  provides to a coding or research agent, on top of a baseline run
  without the skill. It pairs scheme generation, sandboxed task
  execution via Harbor, and an LLM judge that scores both utility
  (capability gain) and security (exploitability of skill contents).
  This repository is the open-source companion to the SkillLens
  arXiv preprint.
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  # FIXME: replace with the real author list and arXiv eprint ID.
  authors:
    - name: "SkillLens-AI Contributors"
  title: >-
    SkillLens: From Task-First Evaluation to Skill-Centered Assessment
  year: 2026
  journal: "arXiv preprint"
